From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] basicswap: BCH electrum (light) mode -- upstream-PR
 candidate core

Teaches the shared electrum plumbing that Bitcoin Cash exists, so BCH can run
"Lean" against public Fulcrum servers with no local chain, the way BTC and LTC
already do. Everything BCH-specific lives in `interface/bch/bch.py` OVERRIDES
or in NEW map entries, so this patch touches no function PWNDA-PATCH-3, -6 or
-7 also touch and stays an independently-appliable upstream-PR candidate.

Contents: eight `bch.py` overrides gain electrum branches; a new
`_signTxWithWalletElectrum` (the FORKID signer -- BCH has no witness, so
btc.py's inherited P2WPKH version cannot be reused); `watch_blocks_for_scripts()`
False in electrum mode; `wallet_manager.py` learns BCH's coin type (145) and
CashAddr derivation; `electrumx.py` gains a live-verified BCH server list;
`bin/prepare.py` registers the `bch` prefix so `--bch-mode` parses.

Three load-bearing bugs found while verifying the "46 inherited methods need
verification, not code" premise, all fixed here: `fundSCLockTx`'s inherited
`require_segwit_inputs=True` filters every BCH UTXO to zero (BCH's "hrp" is a
CashAddr prefix, not a bech32 HRP) and is structurally inapplicable to BCH's
Route-B covenant anyway; `getDestForAddress` falls back to a base58-only
decoder that crashes on CashAddr's ":"; and `scripthash_from_address` fails
the same way for every balance/UTXO query the electrum backend makes.

REVISED 2026-09-03 (Phase E unit E2, running this patch inside a REAL
BasicSwap instance for the first time): `basicswap.py::createInterface()`'s
`Coins.BCH` branch never called `_initElectrumBackend()`, unlike the BTC and
LTC branches beside it -- so `BCHInterface.useBackend()` was permanently False
and a real node crashed immediately after "WalletManager initialized for BCH".
Every prior verification of this patch was source-level or stubbed and could
not have caught it. Fixed by mirroring BTC/LTC exactly.

